{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "neighbor:inventory:categories:001O:example/0001", "hash": "sha256:b630f7601bf0ba480adc5ed28ef820052befb5f68d7e6764385e7d2ed19600c5", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 19085, "byte_start": 18296, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:d4ad7cd4198fc4efca8a37de87ca4f537f9e45615f8a3772cd39b28a605ef9ce", "line_end": 521, "line_start": 491}, "owner_tag": "001O", "parent_tag": "001L", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{example-hom-functor}", "MATH_0001": "$U\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\nh_U & : & \\mathcal{C}\n&\n\\longrightarrow\n&\n\\textit{Sets} \\\\\n& &\nX\n&\n\\longmapsto\n&\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(X, U)\n\\end{matrix}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(X, U)$", "MATH_0005": "$h_U$", "MATH_0006": "$f : X\\to Y$", "MATH_0007": "$h_U(f) : \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(Y, U)\\to \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(X, U)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0009": "$\\phi\\circ f$", "MATH_0010": "$h_U : \\mathcal{C}^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0013": "$U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{example}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{example}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3d10b7039aed038c11d0333703e7e8de20ec703effbe7d43b1f77542503e3968", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b24b5221897408360f06092324539fc71c1fbcc3f080b875c97fd09f16bebac7", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nFunctor of points.\nFor any <MATH_0001> there is a contravariant\nfunctor\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich takes an object <MATH_0003> to the set\n<MATH_0004>. In other words <MATH_0005> is a presheaf.\nGiven a morphism <MATH_0006> the corresponding map\n<MATH_0007>\ntakes <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>. We will always denote\nthis presheaf <MATH_0010>.\nIt is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable presheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> associated to <MATH_0011>.\nIf <MATH_0012> is the category of schemes this functor is\nsometimes referred to as the\n<EMPHOPEN_0001>functor of points<EMPHCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6706795f223adc29c1835d0ee9fcb1e60be6d4a8dcd0c1ceb60373d44b1e65b4", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:001O:example/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "neighbor:inventory:categories:001P:lemma/0001", "hash": "sha256:6d21a07ffa234aedfa63b93cbbb0e65caf1848dd45e43a618af6a62cb77921e4", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 20318, "byte_start": 19691, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:2a5052d951cf1e928456104a391eaabfaf366e9dae4c7b7ae9205d410ed9909a", "line_end": 558, "line_start": 540}, "owner_tag": "001P", "parent_tag": "001L", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"ENVARGEND_0001": "]", "ENVARGOPEN_0001": "[", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-yoneda}", "LOCKED_0002": "\\begin{reference}\nAppeared in some form in \\cite{Yoneda-homology}. Used by Grothendieck in a\ngeneralized form in \\cite{Gr-II}.\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$U, V \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$s : h_U \\to h_V$", "MATH_0003": "$\\phi : U \\to V$", "MATH_0004": "$h(\\phi) = s$", "MATH_0005": "$h$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U, F) \\longrightarrow F(U),\n\\quad\ns \\longmapsto s_U(\\text{id}_U).\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:db993da333ca058eebd298f6661afc328088822e613f5bd0deb7acd3205f86f0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:59f1336290199d42199d776d0d1a2d6d51ffea52fa376b39f101fd3f61bcc6dc", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><ENVARGOPEN_0001>Yoneda lemma<ENVARGEND_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\n<LOCKED_0002>\nLet <MATH_0001>.\nGiven any morphism of functors <MATH_0002>\nthere is a unique morphism <MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004>. In other words the\nfunctor <MATH_0005> is fully faithful. More generally,\ngiven any contravariant functor <MATH_0006> and any object\n<MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008> we have a natural bijection\n<MATH_0009>\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:23f41fdc74b0e5d6190667a6c98e6d852b61adb61e1f8b04209fdb8e393b19bd", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:001P:lemma/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "reference:categories-remark-big-categories", "hash": "sha256:e4ff32bfe40dd9a8596f9bf4d26cbec218b67cf694c27586d649d90c5ea36dce", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 4422, "byte_start": 2478, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:67f8624c8987b067e029d9e39dbd82ed79a8ad52a2cde1960a9e566b5c45b7fe", "line_end": 115, "line_start": 76}, "owner_tag": "0015", "parent_tag": "0013", "requested_label": "categories-remark-big-categories", "requested_tag": "0015", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-big-categories}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Ab}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\textit{Groups}$", "MATH_0006": "$G$", "MATH_0007": "$G\\textit{-Sets}$", "MATH_0008": "$G$", "MATH_0009": "$R$", "MATH_0010": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0011": "$R$", "MATH_0012": "$k$", "MATH_0013": "$k$", "MATH_0014": "$\\textit{Top}$", "MATH_0015": "$X$", "MATH_0016": "$\\textit{PSh}(X)$", "MATH_0017": "$X$", "MATH_0018": "$X$", "MATH_0019": "$\\Sh(X)$", "MATH_0020": "$X$", "MATH_0021": "$X$", "MATH_0022": "$\\textit{PAb}(X)$", "MATH_0023": "$X$", "MATH_0024": "$X$", "MATH_0025": "$\\textit{Ab}(X)$", "MATH_0026": "$X$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0029": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0030": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0032": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0033": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{dpa-section-divided-power-rings}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\item", "STRUCT_0010": "\\item", "STRUCT_0011": "\\item", "STRUCT_0012": "\\item", "STRUCT_0013": "\\item", "STRUCT_0014": "\\item", "STRUCT_0015": "\\item", "STRUCT_0016": "\\item", "STRUCT_0017": "\\item", "STRUCT_0018": "\\item", "STRUCT_0019": "\\item", "STRUCT_0020": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0021": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:75989370749413a256a057563f7b29aba589eb9cfca025fe952ce9239d90193a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:64e50e7c7274b0d327af71b57159b0bb0e4f4ba186eb9f62f3ffa554e03438eb", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nBig categories. In some texts a category is allowed to have a proper\nclass of objects. We will allow this as well in these notes but only\nin the following list of cases (to be updated as we go along).\nIn particular, when we say: ``Let <MATH_0001> be a category''\nthen it is understood that <MATH_0002> is a set.\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> The category <MATH_0003> of sets.\n<STRUCT_0004> The category <MATH_0004> of abelian groups.\n<STRUCT_0005> The category <MATH_0005> of groups.\n<STRUCT_0006> Given a group <MATH_0006> the category <MATH_0007> of\nsets with a left <MATH_0008>-action.\n<STRUCT_0007> Given a ring <MATH_0009> the category <MATH_0010> of <MATH_0011>-modules.\n<STRUCT_0008> Given a field <MATH_0012> the category of vector spaces over <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0009> The category of rings.\n<STRUCT_0010> The category of divided power rings, see\nDivided Power Algebra, Section <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0011> The category of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0012> The category <MATH_0014> of topological spaces.\n<STRUCT_0013> Given a topological space <MATH_0015> the category\n<MATH_0016> of presheaves of sets over <MATH_0017>.\n<STRUCT_0014> Given a topological space <MATH_0018> the category\n<MATH_0019> of sheaves of sets over <MATH_0020>.\n<STRUCT_0015> Given a topological space <MATH_0021> the category\n<MATH_0022> of presheaves of abelian groups over <MATH_0023>.\n<STRUCT_0016> Given a topological space <MATH_0024> the category\n<MATH_0025> of sheaves of abelian groups over <MATH_0026>.\n<STRUCT_0017> Given a small category <MATH_0027> the category of functors\nfrom <MATH_0028> to <MATH_0029>.\n<STRUCT_0018> Given a category <MATH_0030> the category of presheaves of sets\nover <MATH_0031>.\n<STRUCT_0019> Given a site <MATH_0032> the category of sheaves\nof sets over <MATH_0033>.\n<STRUCT_0020>\nOne of the reason to enumerate these here is to try and avoid\nworking with something like the ``collection'' of ``big'' categories\nwhich would be like working with the collection of all classes\nwhich I think definitively is a meta-mathematical object.\n<STRUCT_0021>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9f725712a0349e3d093127a6b4d8aca46e33126abe5ec409bce7f6cf30b2a29", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0015:remark/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "reference:categories-remark-functor-into-sets", "hash": "sha256:10c6907bd6207eaf251a8241a0ce1e82dcfb26b3919672848599bf90796a684a", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 9487, "byte_start": 8912, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:69371291f30f874e05feedf8df575a080aea36891d47a524a500f64b381442cd", "line_end": 244, "line_start": 230}, "owner_tag": "001E", "parent_tag": "0013", "requested_label": "categories-remark-functor-into-sets", "requested_tag": "001E", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-functor-into-sets}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$F(\\Ob(\\mathcal{A}))$", "MATH_0007": "$F$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0009": "$F(\\Ob(\\mathcal{A}))$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-section-sets-everything}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e64a52f350c9be9c00e58701de533b99e4ec9b13f4c17e261ba31132e6624f50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7741349d6621714cc463329d6dd3dd11d0e22551af4f1c52b7399f23684d221b", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nSuppose that <MATH_0001> is a category.\nA functor <MATH_0002> from <MATH_0003> to <MATH_0004>\nis a mathematical object (i.e., it is a set not a class or a formula\nof set theory, see\nSets, Section <REF_0001>)\neven though the category of sets is ``big''.\nNamely, the range of <MATH_0005> on objects will be\na set <MATH_0006> and then we\nmay think of <MATH_0007> as a functor between\n<MATH_0008> and the full subcategory\nof the category of sets whose\nobjects are elements of <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7ec0248f5c19605af7025696e9e38694a10ba978f4e143c969e268e0f3a58ab4", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:001E:remark/0001"}}}], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:225585c173a42b95aaa5fe209795d881fb9d3983319ef8a9b51716c17324b573", "path": "translation-data/source-adoption-inputs/categories-completion-g001-20261020.json"}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:9deca4826c109b52bea8c255d220b80155ca476f753d967ab2205562d366bcf9", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-g001-20261020-retry1-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:242195484a3315e451d035f96488363d71390cb364839effcb54a79a90fde549"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": [], "policy_revision": "git:23ebbe97bcd5e4c5aca1f01bb66a518b8d8b30dd", "prior_generations": [{"candidates": {"hash": "sha256:5df63dd1dfe53e5f5639182d7a3bb01967b3ce3ea3d0387a967cf619c4fabc4e", "path": "translation-data/retired/source-adoptions/categories-completion-g001-20261020-prior-01/candidates.jsonl"}, "generation_inputs": [{"hash": "sha256:c9ef893b184fe4a29930359152f7f7aedbdeac6699f130f3dae2858ab29e0ca4", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p001-frozen.json"}], "raw_outputs": [{"hash": "sha256:d5d94f9ee4d4b467d99498819eacdf4a003cc5c3455a641b247940f090ed45c3", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p001-raw.jsonl"}, {"hash": "sha256:b51262463b01b40e67f8cb5a3e1c13fac9153530a8270cd64d9a3c9091bd3d79", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p001-retry-raw.jsonl"}], "runs": [{"hash": "sha256:0446e3286fe0ea68b0a371b3e6613054beab94586bde8ae24f9038a11d1e7dca", "path": "translation-data/runs/run-20261019-categories-remaining-p001-gpt61sol.json"}], "units": {"hash": "sha256:05058c8b75ce797ebafca8998db7ac95c45a9e47cd191777dc7c8727f69d85e0", "path": "translation-data/retired/source-adoptions/categories-completion-g001-20261020-prior-01/units.jsonl"}}], "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "source_adoption_id": "categories-completion-g001-20261020", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "style_guide_path": "config/style-guide.md", "turn_id": "01a155a4-538d-73b3-bd15-7b1d6b6fd32e", "unit_id": "tag:001L:prose-0004"}, "context_hash": "sha256:60aad58b8a090879326820e48e9b0ce4082d94fe38cce2788d6ab4b13f0578dd", "created_at": "2026-10-19T19:38:41.010153Z", "glossary_revision": "git:23ebbe97bcd5e4c5aca1f01bb66a518b8d8b30dd", "harness_id": "codex", "harness_version": "0.163.0-alpha.10.2", "model_id": "gpt-6.1-sol", "model_identity_confidence": "declared", "model_lane": "openai-gpt-6.1-sol", "model_record_id": "openai:gpt-6.1-sol:declared", "model_snapshot": null, "notes": [], "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "publication_status": "CANDIDATE", "qa_status": "PASS", "reasoning_effort": "high", "run_id": "run-categories-completion-g001-20261020", "schema_version": 2, "source_adoption_id": "categories-completion-g001-20261020", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fadabac157b02ac87b90acebf9dcb3acea85a07760585d986c2629b6c802fb76", "stage": "STRUCTURE_OK", "term_occurrences": [{"source_term": "morphism", "target_term": "态射"}, {"source_term": "functors", "target_term": "函子"}, {"source_term": "natural transformation", "target_term": "自然变换"}, {"source_term": "morphism", "target_term": "态射"}, {"source_term": "composing", "target_term": "复合"}, {"source_term": "morphisms", "target_term": "态射"}, {"source_term": "composition", "target_term": "复合"}, {"source_term": "functors", "target_term": "函子"}, {"source_term": "transformations", "target_term": "变换"}, {"source_term": "composition", "target_term": "复合"}, {"source_term": "functor", "target_term": "函子"}, {"source_term": "target", "target_term": "靶"}, {"source_term": "category", "target_term": "范畴"}, {"source_term": "mathematical object", "target_term": "数学对象"}, {"source_term": "set", "target_term": "集合"}], "term_status": "DECISION_REQUIRED", "translation": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\n注意，给定一个态射（morphism）<MATH_0001>，它位于<MATH_0002>中，我们得到一个相应的函子（functors）间的自然变换（natural transformation）<MATH_0003>，它通过与态射（morphism）<MATH_0004>复合（composing）而定义。这将<MATH_0005>中态射（morphisms）的复合（composition）变为函子（functors）的变换（transformations）的复合（composition）。换言之，我们得到一个函子（functor）\n<MATH_0006>\n注意，其靶（target）是一个“大”的范畴（category），见注记<REF_0001>。另一方面，<MATH_0007>是一个实际的数学对象（mathematical object）（即<SPACE_0001>一个集合（set）），比较注记<REF_0002>。\n\n", "translation_hash": "sha256:82ca31f1572a7ac9ed8dc65f0889dcbfa9dd3191e1d08e8aa2f4cf74e6245b8c", "unit_id": "tag:001L:prose-0004", "unknown_terms": [{"context": "范畴中的态射。", "source_term": "morphism", "target_term": "态射"}, {"context": "自然变换及其复合涉及的函子。", "source_term": "functors", "target_term": "函子"}, {"context": "由给定态射诱导的函子间自然变换。", "source_term": "natural transformation", "target_term": "自然变换"}, {"context": "用于定义自然变换的态射。", "source_term": "morphism", "target_term": "态射"}, {"context": "与给定态射作复合来定义自然变换。", "source_term": "composing", "target_term": "复合"}, {"context": "原范畴中参与复合的态射。", "source_term": "morphisms", "target_term": "态射"}, {"context": "原范畴中态射的复合。", "source_term": "composition", "target_term": "复合"}, {"context": "变换所连接的函子。", "source_term": "functors", "target_term": "函子"}, {"context": "函子之间可作复合的变换。", "source_term": "transformations", "target_term": "变换"}, {"context": "函子之间变换的复合。", "source_term": "composition", "target_term": "复合"}, {"context": "从原范畴到预层范畴的函子。", "source_term": "functor", "target_term": "函子"}, {"context": "所构造函子的靶是大范畴。", "source_term": "target", "target_term": "靶"}, {"context": "函子的靶范畴。", "source_term": "category", "target_term": "范畴"}, {"context": "作为实际集合的函子。", "source_term": "mathematical object", "target_term": "数学对象"}, {"context": "与大范畴相区别的实际集合。", "source_term": "set", "target_term": "集合"}]}
